course: dictionary
lesson: 13968
title: Birds of the hedge and heath
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A linnet is a small brown songbird. It is a noun, so it names a thing: one linnet, or many linnets. «A linnet sat on the hedge and sang a sweet, quick song.» The words hedge and song are clues: a hedge is where birds perch, and a song is what birds make. So a linnet must be a bird that sings.
explain: Writers choose linnets because their song is sweet. Old poems and songs mention them for this reason. «We walked across the heath and heard linnets singing in the gorse.» A heath is a wide, open place with low plants, so the sentence tells you linnets live in hedges and on heaths.
explain: Clues can also tell you about looks. «In spring, the male linnet has a pinkish-red chest and head.» The words in spring and male tell you this is a change that happens at one time of year, and only to the males. The rest of the bird stays brown, so the colour is a clue to the sex of the bird.
fact: A linnet is a small brown songbird of the finch family.
fact: «A linnet sat on the hedge and sang a sweet, quick song.»
fact: In spring, the male linnet has a pinkish-red chest and head.
fact: A hedge is a row of bushes or small trees, and a heath is a wide, open place with low plants.
fact: Linnets are a noun: a linnet, or linnets when there are more than one.
exercise: «A linnet sat on the hedge and sang.» What is a linnet? | A type of hedge | *A small brown songbird | A large black bird that cannot sing | A kind of flower
exercise: «In spring, the male linnet has a pinkish-red chest and head.» Which part of the male turns pinkish-red? | The tail and wings | The whole body | *The chest and head | The legs
exercise: «We walked across the heath and saw linnets.» Find and copy the word that names birds. | heath | walked | *linnets | across
test: Which family of birds is the linnet part of? | Penguins | Eagles | *Finches | Owls
test: «Poets write about linnets for their sweet song.» Why do poets mention linnets? | Because they cannot fly | They are loud and grumpy | *For their sweet song | Because they live in the sea
exam: What does linnet mean? | A red flower | A type of tree | A large sea bird | *A small brown songbird of the finch family
